0..88 Comment "// Two processes run one program, each migration to `far` in the process it is bound to."
89..91 Comment "//"
92..168 Comment "// It witnesses the world bindings: a world names a process only through the"
169..208 Comment "// host\'s binding, never in the source."
209..211 Comment "//"
212..286 Comment "// One process hosts `far` with `gandr host`, and another runs `main` with"
287..366 Comment "// `gandr run`, each given the binding `--world far=<key>@<ip:port>`. The first"
367..445 Comment "// migration holds 42 at `far`. The second reads it there again, a capture the"
446..521 Comment "// hosting process already holds, so nothing is fetched. With no `--world`,"
522..581 Comment "// both migrations run in this process and answer the same."
582..584 Comment "//"
585..653 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/net.rs` — the two processes"
654..717 Comment "// - see: `twice.gandr` — the same migrations, in one process"
718..791 Comment "// - see: `corpus/pathological/worlds/open.gandr` — a thunk that cannot"
792..802 Comment "//   cross"
